.SH NAME
hed\-dired \- A directory browser inspired by oil.nvim: opening a
directory drops you into a buffer where each line is a directory entry.
Navigate with your normal motions, hit  to descend or open a file.
.PP
A directory browser inspired by \f[CR]oil.nvim\f[R]: opening a directory
drops you into a buffer where each line is a directory entry.
Navigate with your normal motions, hit \f[CR]<CR>\f[R] to descend or
open a file.
.SH Usage
.IP
.EX
:e .              # open current directory in dired
:e some/dir       # open a specific directory
.EE
.PP
Any time \f[CR]:e\f[R] is given a directory, dired claims the open via
the \f[CR]HOOK_BUFFER_OPEN_PRE\f[R] intercept and renders the listing
instead of core\[cq]s default file\-open path.
.SH Keybinds (NORMAL mode, dired buffer only)
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
T{
Key
T}@T{
Action
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]<CR>\f[R]
T}@T{
Open the entry under the cursor (file or subdir)
T}
T{
\f[CR]\-\f[R]
T}@T{
Go to parent directory
T}
T{
\f[CR]\[ti]\f[R]
T}@T{
Go to \f[CR]$HOME\f[R]
T}
T{
\f[CR]cd\f[R]
T}@T{
Change hed\[cq]s cwd to this directory
T}
.TE
.PP
\f[CR]hjkl\f[R], \f[CR]gg\f[R], \f[CR]G\f[R], search, etc.
all work \[em] it\[cq]s a normal buffer.
.SH Display
Each line renders as \f[CR]<type\-marker> <name>\f[R]:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]d\f[R] \[em] directory
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]l\f[R] \[em] symlink (target shown after \f[CR]\->\f[R])
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\f[R] \[em] regular file
.PP
Hidden entries (starting with \f[CR].\f[R]) are shown.
.SH Notes
The dired buffer is read\-only \[em] you can\[cq]t rename or delete
entries by editing the listing (yet).
Use \f[CR]:shell\f[R] for filesystem operations.
